    {
      "id": 101339,
      "name": "BlueHairedMeerkat",
      "username": "BlueHairedMeerkat",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bluehairedmeerkat/{size}/1967_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-05-06T17:49:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>How ridiculous. I approve :D</p><p>I shall try this, with Legacy. Don't know how I'm going to manage the Legacy Ring, but still...</p><p>EDIT: I'll also take a crack at difficulties, if you like.</p><ul>\n<li>Absolute Zero: 15 unique cards, and I defy anyone to fit Null-Point Calibration Unit or Isothermic Transducer into casual conversation.&nbsp;<strong>HARD.</strong>\n</li>\n<li>Argent Adept: 20 unique cards, and many proper nouns.&nbsp;<strong>VERY HARD.</strong>\n</li>\n<li>Bunker: 14 unique cards, lots of military stuff. Not straightforward, but not too many tricky ones.&nbsp;<strong>AVERAGE.</strong>\n</li>\n<li>Chrono-Ranger: 20 unique cards, but Jim's Hat and the Masadah are probably the only problematic ones, and the bounties should be no problem.&nbsp;<strong>AVERAGE.</strong>\n</li>\n<li>Expatriette: 17 unique cards, but these are all actual things.&nbsp;<strong>VERY EASY.</strong>\n</li>\n<li>Fanatic: 18 unique cards. Some (\"SMITE THE TRANSGRESSOR!\") will be easy, but there are a couple of pitfalls.&nbsp;<strong>EASY.</strong>\n</li>\n<li>Haka: 14 unique cards. Easy if you're Maori(?), otherwise not so much. Though Taiaha is a fun onomatopoeia...&nbsp;<strong>HARD.</strong>\n</li>\n<li>Legacy: 15 unique cards, and The Legacy Ring is the only one that'll slow you down.&nbsp;<strong>VERY EASY.</strong>\n</li>\n<li>Mr. Fixer: 17 unique cards. The tools are probably okay, and maybe the styles if you're creative with it.&nbsp;<strong>EASY.</strong>\n</li>\n<li>Nightmist: 16 unique cards, some of them fairly tricky, others less so.&nbsp;<strong>AVERAGE.</strong>\n</li>\n<li>Omnitron-X: 17 unique cards, and most of them are pretty nasty.&nbsp;<strong>HARD.</strong>\n</li>\n<li>Ra: 15 unique cards, and the Staff is probably the only tricky one. <b>VERY EASY.</b>\n</li>\n<li>Scholar: 16 unique cards. The Forms might be tricky, but the rest should be okay.&nbsp;<strong>EASY.</strong>\n</li>\n<li>Tachyon: 15 unique cards. A lot of not easy, but nothing terrible.&nbsp;<strong>AVERAGE.</strong>\n</li>\n<li>Tempest: 16 unique cards. Elemental Subwave Inducer could be tricky, but most of the others are fine.&nbsp;<strong>EASY.</strong>\n</li>\n<li>Unity: 19 unique cards, and most of them are robots, which might be tricky.&nbsp;<strong>HARD.</strong>\n</li>\n<li>Visionary: 15 unique cards, and Twist The Ether is probably the only real problem. <b>VERY EASY.</b>\n</li>\n<li>Wraith: 15 unique cards, mostly pretty easy.&nbsp;<strong>EASY.</strong>\n</li>\n</ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Vengeance later, possibly.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>[I also picked up a couple of typos on the full card spoiler, which I'm putting here instead of in the proper place because I'm trying to leave and don't want to forget them: Planar Banishment is Planar Punishment and Expect The Worst is Expect The Worse]</p>",
